/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 567 0 R
/T (Parkinson's disease is a progressive neurological condition characterized by tremors, stiffness, and impaired movement. It also presents non-motor symptoms like cognitive decline and mood changes. Over time, symptoms worsen, affecting daily activities and quality of life. While the exact cause is unclear, it involves the loss of dopamine-producing neurons in the brain. Treatment aims to alleviate symptoms through medication, therapy, and lifestyle adjustments. Despite ongoing research, Parkinson's remains incurable, highlighting the importance of continued efforts in understanding and managing the disease.)
/E (Parkinson's disease is a progressive neurological condition characterized by tremors, stiffness, and impaired movement. It also presents non-motor symptoms like cognitive decline and mood changes. Over time, symptoms worsen, affecting daily activities and quality of life. While the exact cause is unclear, it involves the loss of dopamine-producing neurons in the brain. Treatment aims to alleviate symptoms through medication, therapy, and lifestyle adjustments. Despite ongoing research, Parkinson's remains incurable, highlighting the importance of continued efforts in understanding and managing the disease.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
