877 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 572 0 R
/E (diagnosis, motor symptoms escalate, with bradykinesia, tremor, and rigidity worsening. Urinary dysfunction arises at the 10-year mark, followed by gait instability, falls, and cognitive decline at 20 years post-diagnosis. These manifestations  correspond  to   the  loss of dopaminergic neurons in the substantia nigra pars compacta. As the disease advances, dysphagia, freezing of gait, and psychiatric symptoms like hallucinations and obsessive-compulsive behaviors become pronounced. Understanding this progressive trajectory is crucial for tailoring interventions and managing the multifaceted manifestations of Parkinson's disease effectively.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
