/T (The baseline assessment serves as a crucial reference point for monitoring disease progression and evaluating treatment efficacy over time. By establishing a comprehensive baseline profile of PD patients, clinicians can track changes in symptoms, functional abilities, and medication responses longitudinally. Furthermore, the identification of baseline predictors, such as age, disease duration, and genetic factors, enables personalized management strategies tailored to individual patient needs. Through regular reassessment and comparison with baseline data, clinicians can refine treatment approaches, optimize symptom management, and improve overall patient outcomes in the management of Parkinson's disease.)
/E (The baseline assessment serves as a crucial reference point for monitoring disease progression and evaluating treatment efficacy over time. By establishing a comprehensive baseline profile of PD patients, clinicians can track changes in symptoms, functional abilities, and medication responses longitudinally. Furthermore, the identification of baseline predictors, such as age, disease duration, and genetic factors, enables personalized management strategies tailored to individual patient needs. Through regular reassessment and comparison with baseline data, clinicians can refine treatment approaches, optimize symptom management, and improve overall patient outcomes in the management of Parkinson's disease.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [9]
>>
