/Title (The findings indicate the relative importance of different features in influencing Parkinson's disease progression. Motor function assessments such as Finger Tapping Speed, UPDRS Part III score, and mobility tests like the 10-meter walk and TUG tests demonstrate high importance. Genetic testing results for specific mutations, age, and sex also influence disease progression. Additionally, cognitive and functional measures, medication dosages, and comorbidity profiles play significant roles. Understanding these factors aids in developing targeted interventions for PD management.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4256 0 R
