/Title (After conducting the time series analysis, we observed fluctuations in UPDRS Part III scores over time, indicating variations in motor symptom severity among patients with Parkinson's disease. Some individuals showed gradual progression with increasing UPDRS scores over time, suggesting worsening of motor symptoms. Conversely, a few patients exhibited periods of stability or even improvement in UPDRS scores, potentially reflecting treatment efficacy or natural fluctuations in symptom severity. Overall, the analysis highlights the heterogeneous nature of Parkinson's disease progression and underscores the importance of personalized treatment approaches.)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4490 0 R
